## Limitations

- Tokens are estimated as bytes/4. Category shares compare estimates with estimates and do not depend on the constant; the context-impact share divides an estimate by real token counts, so it scales with the constant (about 33% low if the true ratio is 3 bytes per token).
- Transcripts are what Claude Code stores, not the exact requests sent to the API.
- Only the history Claude Code keeps (30 days by default) is analysed.
- The policy is conservative: a Bash command that reads or searches anywhere passes through entirely.
